    "problem_statement": "Ok.unwrap_or() returns default value when value is not None\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `unwrap_or()` method on `Ok` instances is incorrectly returning the default value when the wrapped value is not None, instead of returning the actual wrapped value.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom result import Ok\n\n# This should return 'yay' but returns 'some_default' instead\nok_result = Ok('yay')\nvalue = ok_result.unwrap_or('some_default')\nprint(f\"Expected: 'yay', Got: '{value}'\")\n\n# This also fails - should return the actual value, not the default\nok_with_number = Ok(42)\nnumber = ok_with_number.unwrap_or(0)\nprint(f\"Expected: 42, Got: {number}\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nExpected: 'yay', Got: 'yay'\nExpected: 42, Got: 42\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nExpected: 'yay', Got: 'some_default'\nExpected: 42, Got: 0\n```\n\nThe method should only return the default value when dealing with `Err` instances, not `Ok` instances."
